Hello, 

I'll give the useless opinion of someone on holiday. As long as you are not using a weighting scheme based on the inverse spatial distance, you should be fine. Some graphs deal poorly with duplicated locations though  (Delaunay, Gabriel). Neighbourhood based on a distance threshold, or K nearest neighbours are probably better options. 

As for your analysis using 35 vs 68 sites, well, yes the PCNM will be different as these are different data. If you have a few highly sampled locations then Valeria's suggestion is worth trying too.

Cheers

