I will give you the useless opinion of someone working at 9pm on a Friday night. I guess the difference here could be made by the spatial matrix you are using. If it's a connectivity matrix, the binary code will consider the inds from the same locations as neighbours and won't really mind about them having the same coordinates. If you are otherwise using a weighted matrix, I suppose that having the same weights associated to different quantitative variables may be a confusing information, more than redundant. In this second case I would probably calculate the gene frequencies for all the inds at each site as they were pops and perform the spatial analysis on it...that's all that comes to my mind.

